<Prose title="Privacy Policy" description="HostDeck doesn't collect, store or share any personal data." updated="25 October 2026">
  <p><strong>HostDeck does not collect, store or share any personal data.</strong> This applies to both editions: the Mac App Store version and the direct download.</p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No network access.</strong> HostDeck makes no network connections of its own. Commands you run (for
      example <code>ssh</code>) are run by your terminal app, and file-transfer hosts are opened by your file-transfer
      app, not by HostDeck.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local data only.</strong> Your hosts, settings and global shortcut are stored on your Mac in HostDeck’s
      Application Support folder. Recently used commands, how often you use them (to rank search results), a few display
      choices and, if you grant it, access to your <code>.ssh</code> folder are remembered in HostDeck’s preferences on
      your Mac. None of it leaves your Mac.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No passwords.</strong> HostDeck never asks for, stores or sends passwords. SSH sign-in is handled by ssh and
      your keys; file-transfer apps ask for passwords themselves and keep them in their own keychain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Files you choose.</strong> HostDeck reads <code>~/.ssh/config</code> (and the files it includes) to list
      your SSH hosts and to work out where “Browse Files” connects. The Mac App Store version only does so after you
      allow access to your <code>.ssh</code> folder. HostDeck only imports or exports config files you pick in an Open
      or Save dialog.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Opening commands.</strong> HostDeck only acts on the command you choose from its menu. The Mac App Store
      version opens SSH hosts as ssh:// links in Terminal or iTerm2 and copies other commands to your clipboard. The
      direct download, with your permission, asks Terminal or iTerm2 to run the command. File-transfer hosts are
      handed to the file-transfer app you choose. HostDeck never runs commands on its own.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clipboard.</strong> HostDeck writes to the clipboard only when you choose an action that copies (such as
      Copy Command), and reads it only when you paste into one of its fields.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No analytics, tracking or advertising.</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website has no cookies, analytics or tracking. It’s hosted by GitHub Pages, which may log visitors’ IP
    addresses for security, as described in
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Ask on the <a href={site.supportUrl}>HostDeck support page on GitHub</a>.</p>
</Prose>
